<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Bounty Hunters</h1>
<p>The Bounty Hunters Guild lies north of the King's Road. In its Contracts 
Room, west of the hall, the Hunter hands out contracts on monsters all over 
the world. You must be level 50 or higher to take one.
</p><p>Usage (in front of the Hunter):
</p>
<pre>say daily contract       a new target, to be killed today
say monthly contract     a target for this month, for a bigger reward
say bonus contract       an extra target, with no time limit
say contract status      your open contracts
say report               your totals and streaks
</pre>
<p>The target is a monster anywhere in the world. Kill it, <a cmd='#'>decapitate</a> the 
corpse and give the head to the Hunter. A daily contract only counts on 
the day it was given, a monthly one only in its month. You hold one 
contract of each kind at a time.
</p><p>Each contract closed pays experience and money, and bounty points (BP), 
which you spend in the guild shop (<a cmd='#'>list</a>, <a cmd='#'>buy</a>). The reward grows with 
your streak, the number of contracts of a kind you have closed in a row, 
and doubles on milestones: a daily streak of 14, 30, 60, 90, 180 or 365, a 
monthly streak of 6, 12, 18 or 24. Miss a day (or a month), or leave a 
contract unfinished, and that streak starts over. Logging in on days in a 
row also earns BP.
</p><p>From the shop:
</p>
<ul><li>The <b>tablet</b> keeps all your contracts in one place (<a cmd='#'>look tablet</a>); with it, the Hunter updates the tablet instead of handing you papers.</li>
<li>A <b>contract breaking note</b> lets you drop a daily or monthly contract without losing your streak: give it to the Hunter and say daily or monthly.</li>
<li>A <b>hint</b> (<a cmd='#'>look hint</a>) tells you in which zone or land your target is.</li></ul>
<p>Giving up a bonus contract costs 25,000 experience and 5 BP.
</p><p>The guild has more for veterans: the Jeweler sends you to deliver packages, 
the Blacksmith leads killing sprees for groups, and in time the Historian, 
the Summoner and the Necromancer have their own tasks.
</p><p>Once you have closed 30 daily contracts, the Hunter asks whether you think 
yourself worthy of joining the guild; nod, and the way in begins at the 
Hunters Shrine and leads to the Historian in the library. The Blacksmith, 
the Jeweler, the Summoner and the Necromancer each set you a task; finish 
all four, and the Historian has one last trial for you. Win it, and you are 
a Bounty Hunter, and may sign the tome so the histories speak of you. If you 
fall, you can try the trial again.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
